From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mina Her <minacle@live.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 08:35:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Configure application time zone via environment variable

- Update config/application.rb to read DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE from environment
- Apply custom time zone only if the environment variable is present
- Document the new configuration option in .env.production.sample

Rationale: Allowing administrators to define the application time zone via environment variables improves flexibility for deployment across different regions without requiring code changes.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/.env.production.sample b/.env.production.sample
index 9ff63c49ef..ade2bccc07 100644
--- a/.env.production.sample
+++ b/.env.production.sample
@@ -16,6 +16,12 @@
 # ----------
 LOCAL_DOMAIN=example.com
 
+# Localization
+# ------------
+# Set this to override the Rails application time zone. Leave unset to keep the
+# Rails default.
+# DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE=
+
 # Redis
 # -----
 REDIS_HOST=localhost
diff --git a/config/application.rb b/config/application.rb
index 90cfe47428..eb6cb5417a 100644
--- a/config/application.rb
+++ b/config/application.rb
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@ module Mastodon
     # in config/environments, which are processed later.
     #
     # config.time_zone = "Central Time (US & Canada)"
+    config.time_zone = ENV['DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE'] if ENV.key?('DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE')
     # config.eager_load_paths << Rails.root.join("extras")
 
     # config.paths.add File.join('app', 'api'), glob: File.join('**', '*.rb')
